   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Did anybody runs INLA on big data sets in the cluster",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r<br>You can try adding\r<br>\r<br>control.inla = list(int.strategy = &quot;eb&quot;, control.vb =\r<br>list(f.enable.limit = 2)), \r<br> \r<br>\r<br>as the default &#39;f.enable.limit&#39; is a bit large with that many\r<br>replications. \r<br>\r<br>runs in less than 2 minutes here.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On Thu, 2024-02-01 at 12:16 -0800, T wrote:\r<br>&gt; here is the code \r<br>&gt; load(&#39;climate_sentiment_last_last_with_new_Columns_indices.RData&#39;)\r<br>&gt; ls()\r<br>&gt; df\r<br>&gt; T3 &lt;- sum(df$NTw) / sum(df$TTw)\r<br>&gt; df$E &lt;- df$TTw*T3\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; #When we run the model for more than two years \r<br>&gt; df$FID_2 &lt;- df$FID\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; # Sort data1 by year, month and week\r<br>&gt; library(dplyr)\r<br>&gt; df &lt;- df %&gt;% arrange(year_idx, month_idx, week_idx)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; formula1 &lt;- NTw ~ -1 + f(FID, model = &quot;iid&quot;, # FID_1, random effect in\r<br>&gt; time weeks\r<br>&gt;                                group = week_idx,\r<br>&gt;                                control.group=list(model=&#39;iid&#39;),\r<br>&gt;                                constr = FALSE) +\r<br>&gt;                          f(FID_2, model = &quot;iid&quot;, # FID_2, random\r<br>&gt; effect in time years\r<br>&gt;                          group = year_idx,\r<br>&gt;                          control.group=list(model=&#39;iid&#39;),\r<br>&gt;                          constr = FALSE)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;       time_variable1 &lt;- c(&quot;week_idx&quot;, &quot;year_idx&quot;)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; library(INLA)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; res &lt;- inla(formula1, family = &quot;poisson&quot;, data = df, E = df$E,\r<br>&gt;                 control.predictor = list(compute = TRUE),\r<br>&gt;                 control.compute = list(config = TRUE))\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; res &lt;- summary(res)\r<br>&gt; save(res, file = &quot;summary_data_model1.RData&quot;)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; On Thursday, February 1, 2024 at 6:34:37 PM UTC+1 Helpdesk (Haavard\r<br>&gt; Rue) wrote:\r<br>&gt; &gt; I can rerun it here to check. you do not give much information...\r<br>&gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; On Thu, 2024-02-01 at 07:46 -0800, T wrote:\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; I try to run my model for 8 years big data and every time it get\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; crushed. Do you have any tips?\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; Thanks\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; -- \r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; Groups &quot;R-inla discussion group&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it,\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; send\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">r-inla-discussion...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; To view this discussion on the web, visit\r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/r-inla-discussion-group/b10bb4ea-9d99-4460-9a80-b5c86dbefbdfn%40googlegroups.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/r-inla-discussion-group/b10bb4ea-9d99-4460-9a80-b5c86dbefbdfn%2540googlegroups.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792435858235000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0BPdHl0lanBmom80g6Pk1u\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/r-inla-discussion-group/b10bb4ea-9d99-4460-9a80-b5c86dbefbdfn%40googlegroups.com</a>\r<br>&gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; \r<br>&gt; &gt; &gt; .\r<br>&gt; &gt; \r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br>Håvard Rue\r<br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">he...@r-inla.org</a>\r<br>"
